From afa60d9651beb9765f61d71e600fbd66afe8053c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kel Modderman <kelvmod@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:04:49 +1000
Subject: [application] Drop the 200 ms sleep at the end of
 CApplication::Stop()

The sleep comes from 15dcb7b091 (2011), when Stop() ended with
Destroy() and the process could exit() straight after it, so threads
were given a moment to go away. Destroy() is no longer called there,
and every caller of Stop() now runs Cleanup() afterwards: the Run()
loop, the error paths in XBMC_Run(), the tvOS controller and the WASM
iteration. The sleep only delays Cleanup() by 200 ms on every exit.

Timed on Linux, "Application stopped" to the next main thread line
went from 200 ms to 0-1 ms.

Assisted-By: Claude
(cherry picked from commit aa7ec424e85933fd1e38a3343c35e619340852fb)
---
 xbmc/application/Application.cpp | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/application/Application.cpp b/xbmc/application/Application.cpp
index 95c2bbfa2a..ceee0536d4 100644
--- a/xbmc/application/Application.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/application/Application.cpp
@@ -1960,8 +1960,6 @@ bool CApplication::Stop(int exitCode)
 
   cleanup_emu_environ();
 
-  KODI::TIME::Sleep(200ms);
-
   return success;
 }
 
